prompts.run:
Use the attached EXISTING 2D EAVE RUNNER SPRITE as an exact character and style reference. Produce its hand-drawn EIGHT-FRAME RUN CYCLE SPRITE SHEET, genuine alpha transparent background. One character repeated in eight animation drawings; no other objects or characters. Preserve exactly the same ivory cracked narrow-eye mask, hood, short blue scarf tails, indigo chest wraps, short waist tabs, cord belt and knee knots, baggy charcoal cropped trousers, woven cord arms/shins, brown bamboo forearm bracers, articulated five-finger cord hands and bound sandals. Same lean adult proportions, same head size, same large graphic shapes, same colors and line/shading style. Do not redesign.

LAYOUT: EXACTLY FOUR COLUMNS by TWO ROWS, eight equal square-ish portrait cells across a 3:2 landscape sheet. Transparent gutters. Every whole character plus scarf and dagger fits inside its OWN cell, with ample empty margin. No clipping. Uniform character scale across all frames, constant pelvis center within each cell and identical ground baseline. Sequential animation is left to right top row then bottom row. No labels, numbers, text, borders, checkers, floor, shadows, glow or scenic background.

DIRECTION: every drawing is a SCREEN-RIGHT-FACING side view, with just enough slight three-quarter view to read the mask. Head and torso point right, two cloth tails stream behind toward LEFT. NO front/back views or camera rotation. RUN IN PLACE; no translating through a cell.

EIGHT DISTINCT ANATOMICAL RUN POSES, smooth looping cycle at 12fps:
1 contact: right foot forward to right and left leg extended back to left, low forward lean;
2 down: right knee compresses under weight, rear heel lifts;
3 passing: left knee drives forward, right foot under hip;
4 up/flight: left knee forward high, right leg trails, both feet just above ground;
5 opposite contact: LEFT foot now forward and RIGHT leg extended behind;
6 opposite down: left knee compresses and right rear heel lifts;
7 opposite passing: right knee drives forward, left foot under hip;
8 opposite up/flight: right knee high forward, left leg trails, transitions cleanly into frame1.
Maintain exactly TWO arms, TWO legs, TWO hands, TWO feet in every frame. Both leg phases must visibly alternate. Coherent shoulder/hip counterrotation and restrained body bob, head stable and looking right. Anatomical RIGHT hand carries the same one SHORT steel dagger from the reference in a compact safe low grip; no enormous weapon, duplicate blade, blade merging into legs, or long sword. Free hand swings opposite front leg. Scarf follows the run with a slight delayed bounce, volume and garment construction consistent in every frame.

ART: match reference's detailed but controlled hand-drawn 2D sprite style: heavy near-black outer ink silhouette, thinner interior ink, broad subdued indigo/charcoal cloth values, warm tan bindings, ivory mask, a few selective weave marks and chips. Crisp antialiased edges, two to three clear material shades. Not 3D, not pixel art, not chibi, no smear/blur. Gameplay legibility at 180 pixels tall. Make a usable real run-cycle sheet rather than eight similar idle poses.

prompts.slash:
Animate the EXACT Eave Runner in the attached sprite as a hand-drawn 2D eight-frame RIGHTWARD SHORT-DAGGER SLASH ATTACK. Real alpha transparent background. Exact same character, clothing, mask, proportions, palette, black contour and thin inner ink detail. This is a sprite animation asset, not a poster, not 3D, not pixel art. No text, labels, panels, grid lines, scenery, floor or cast shadow.

OUTPUT: EXACTLY FOUR COLUMNS by TWO ROWS, eight equal cells, landscape 3:2 sheet. Uniform scale and same virtual floor baseline in every cell. Full complete body, hands, feet, scarf and blade within each cell with generous transparent margins. Reading order left to right then second row. Character always faces SCREEN RIGHT in the same side/slight three-quarter game camera, no turns toward viewer, no back view or reversal.

Keep all recognizable features: slim cord-limbed woven ninja, cracked ivory pointed oval mask with thin black eye slits and tiny cyan eye glints, paired-loop forehead emblem, close muted indigo hood, short twin scarf tails trailing LEFT, layered blue diagonal chest wraps and charcoal undershirt, tan rope belt and knots, asymmetric short waist tabs, baggy cropped charcoal trousers ending at knotted knees, thin dark braided cord shins, dark bound sandals, fitted wooden bamboo forearm bracers. Two arms and two legs, consistently articulated hands. No human skin or bones. Same one SHORT steel dagger in the anatomical RIGHT hand throughout, steel blade stays short, no weapon switching hands or disappearing, no second weapon.

EIGHT CLEAR ANIMATION KEYS with a readable anticipation, fast strike and recovery:
1 ready: bent-knee stable guard, right hand holds dagger low, free left hand balances;
2 anticipation: sink lower and coil torso, dagger hand pulls back near hip toward LEFT, scarf starts rising;
3 last windup: low coiled pose, front foot poised to step RIGHT, dagger hand still back, free hand forward;
4 STRIKE: strong short rightward step/lunge, torso leans right, dagger arm extends toward RIGHT in one decisive low-to-mid slicing cut, rear leg pushes off LEFT. This is the widest pose, fit it inside cell;
5 FOLLOW THROUGH: dagger finishes slightly down and across in front, torso remains low and right, trailing scarf snaps LEFT. Add only a thin small ivory blade stroke at the actual dagger arc on frames4 and5, not a big magical crescent;
6 SETTLE: stance compresses after lunge, dagger still in right hand forward and low, no extra strike;
7 RECOVER: torso rises back toward ready, back foot gathers, right dagger hand returns toward low guard;
8 READY AGAIN: return close to frame1 position, ready for next loop.

Stable mask/hood volume and torso length, grounded feet with convincing weight, whole body motion not just waving an arm. Maintain two-to-three clean shade values per material. Selective worn edges and woven marks, controlled detail matching the input. Keep all frames consistent and distinctly timed rather than eight similar poses. Transparent negative space must separate limbs and dagger from body.
